1
00:01:38,120 --> 00:01:39,760
You're really moving too fast.

2
00:01:39,879 --> 00:01:41,000
Developing too quickly.

3
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:42,439
I'm worried I can't keep up with you.

4
00:01:42,640 --> 00:01:44,000
Working with Jinlan all these years,

5
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:46,319
you must have become quite smooth and worldly.

6
00:01:46,560 --> 00:01:47,719
You could easily be a general manager.

7
00:01:47,799 --> 00:01:48,359
Am I right?

8
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:51,040
The travel agency has hundreds of employees.

9
00:01:51,239 --> 00:01:52,879
Jinlan is usually busy with her things,

10
00:01:52,959 --> 00:01:54,239
and I'm busy with mine.

11
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:55,480
We don't cross paths that much.

12
00:01:57,799 --> 00:01:59,719
I'll answer it myself.

13
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:03,599
Hello, please go ahead.

14
00:02:05,159 --> 00:02:06,079
Hold on a moment.

15
00:02:07,879 --> 00:02:09,000
Could you step out for a moment?

16
00:02:52,199 --> 00:02:55,560
Mayor Xie will be promoted and reassigned.

17
00:02:55,560 --> 00:02:57,080
He's about to become chairman.

18
00:02:57,080 --> 00:02:58,120
Have you heard?

19
00:02:58,280 --> 00:02:59,719
Word started going around a month ago.

20
00:03:00,319 --> 00:03:01,680
Many said it was just a rumor.

21
00:03:02,319 --> 00:03:04,879
I'm 80 to 90 percent sure it's true.

22
00:03:05,120 --> 00:03:06,960
His new post is crucial.

23
00:03:07,599 --> 00:03:08,639
Plan ahead.

24
00:03:08,919 --> 00:03:12,039
Start making the right friends early on.

25
00:03:12,199 --> 00:03:12,919
Understood.

26
00:03:21,280 --> 00:03:23,719
Listen, brother, I heard...

27
00:03:23,719 --> 00:03:26,759
Is Mayor Xie's mother back from Beijing?

28
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:29,599
Is she staying at his sister's place now?

29
00:03:48,639 --> 00:03:49,439
Everyone,

30
00:03:49,439 --> 00:03:51,719
The municipal symposium on optimizing

31
00:03:51,719 --> 00:03:54,199
business environments and private firms

32
00:03:54,280 --> 00:03:55,439
will now begin.

33
00:03:55,560 --> 00:03:57,919
Please welcome Mayor Xie for his address.

34
00:04:00,960 --> 00:04:03,120
Comrades from the TV station,

35
00:04:03,120 --> 00:04:04,439
please stop recording for now.

36
00:04:04,439 --> 00:04:07,039
Let's clear up a minor issue first.

37
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:09,120
A while back,

38
00:04:09,120 --> 00:04:11,960
after my mother's medical trip to Beijing,

39
00:04:12,159 --> 00:04:15,960
many comrades went to my sister's place

40
00:04:15,960 --> 00:04:17,399
to drop off money and pay their respects.

41
00:04:17,800 --> 00:04:18,480
The day before yesterday,

42
00:04:18,879 --> 00:04:20,560
right here in this conference room,

43
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:22,000
I made my stance crystal clear.

44
00:04:22,120 --> 00:04:23,240
I appreciate the thought,

45
00:04:23,439 --> 00:04:25,240
but I absolutely cannot accept the money.

46
00:04:25,920 --> 00:04:27,439
I gave everyone three days.

47
00:04:27,759 --> 00:04:29,240
To save you all some face,

48
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:32,120
the money was kept at my sister's house.

49
00:04:32,600 --> 00:04:33,759
If it's your own money,

50
00:04:33,839 --> 00:04:36,199
take it back home to your wife.

51
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:37,800
If it belongs to your company,

52
00:04:37,920 --> 00:04:39,480
hand it over to accounting.

53
00:04:39,879 --> 00:04:41,319
Yet, a select few people,

54
00:04:41,759 --> 00:04:44,439
including some entrepreneurs here today,

55
00:04:44,680 --> 00:04:45,759
have so far

56
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:47,240
not taken their money back.

57
00:04:47,879 --> 00:04:50,279
If you haven't collected it by tonight,

58
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:53,879
I will turn it over to the city treasury.

59
00:04:54,279 --> 00:04:57,160
These rumors are getting out of hand.

60
00:04:57,639 --> 00:04:58,800
Even the provincial leaders have heard.

61
00:04:59,120 --> 00:05:01,040
A provincial leader called me,

62
00:05:01,480 --> 00:05:03,000
claiming I took over a million

63
00:05:03,120 --> 00:05:04,360
and only returned a fraction of it,

64
00:05:04,759 --> 00:05:05,839
saying I'm just putting on a show.

65
00:05:06,560 --> 00:05:08,079
At that time, I responded with four words:

66
00:05:08,959 --> 00:05:10,120
"A clear conscience."

67
00:05:11,319 --> 00:05:12,279
As long as my conscience is clear,

68
00:05:12,959 --> 00:05:15,079
I, Xie Fengshi, fear nothing.

69
00:05:23,720 --> 00:05:25,480
All right, let's officially begin.

70
00:05:25,759 --> 00:05:27,639
Regarding concerns raised by some firms

71
00:05:27,720 --> 00:05:29,399
about certain government departments'

72
00:05:29,399 --> 00:05:30,560
level of cooperation,

73
00:05:30,560 --> 00:05:32,240
minor adjustments need to be made.

74
00:05:33,959 --> 00:05:34,600
Sir,

75
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:37,519
I don't know much about this industry.

76
00:05:39,759 --> 00:05:40,240
Understood.

77
00:05:40,639 --> 00:05:42,800
First, thank you for trusting me.

78
00:05:43,240 --> 00:05:45,120
Second, I'd like to state my commitment:

79
00:05:45,680 --> 00:05:46,639
I'll learn on the job,

80
00:05:46,920 --> 00:05:47,920
and guarantee the task will be completed.

81
00:05:48,279 --> 00:05:49,000
Right.

82
00:05:49,560 --> 00:05:50,319
Rest assured, sir.

83
00:05:51,279 --> 00:05:52,120
All right, see you next week.

84
00:05:52,399 --> 00:05:52,920
Yes, absolutely.

85
00:05:54,879 --> 00:05:57,079
Xiao Lin, you did very well this time.

86
00:05:57,240 --> 00:05:58,399
As an entrepreneur,

87
00:05:58,600 --> 00:06:00,399
you were the first to retrieve your money.

88
00:06:00,600 --> 00:06:02,319
Setting such an example is very important.

89
00:06:02,480 --> 00:06:03,279
Come, have some tea.

90
00:06:03,560 --> 00:06:04,279
Mayor,

91
00:06:05,120 --> 00:06:07,160
I am truly impressed.

92
00:06:07,439 --> 00:06:08,639
I was among the first on the mainland,

93
00:06:09,040 --> 00:06:11,199
and I've never seen anyone quite like you,

94
00:06:11,279 --> 00:06:12,360
who truly honors his word.

95
00:06:12,720 --> 00:06:14,279
Regardless of what anyone else does,

96
00:06:14,279 --> 00:06:16,079
I will definitely follow your lead

97
00:06:16,079 --> 00:06:16,920
and heed your command.

98
00:06:19,040 --> 00:06:19,519
Have some tea.

99
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:24,240
I know.

100
00:06:24,319 --> 00:06:24,720
All right.

101
00:06:24,720 --> 00:06:26,399
I'm in the dorm. Come by later.

102
00:06:28,560 --> 00:06:29,519
Come, drink your tea.

103
00:06:29,519 --> 00:06:30,079
Thank you.

104
00:06:31,519 --> 00:06:32,199
You're so busy.

105
00:06:39,160 --> 00:06:40,800
This hasn't been announced yet.

106
00:06:40,920 --> 00:06:42,879
Isn't it a bit early for congratulations?

107
00:06:45,839 --> 00:06:46,839
I know, I know.

108
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:48,680
All right.

109
00:06:49,959 --> 00:06:50,879
I know what I'm doing.

110
00:06:50,879 --> 00:06:51,600
Don't worry.

111
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:55,480
Sir,

112
00:06:55,480 --> 00:06:56,319
I won't disturb you any longer.

113
00:06:56,319 --> 00:06:57,279
I'll take my leave now.

114
00:06:57,839 --> 00:06:58,879
Congrats in advance on your promotion.

115
00:06:59,680 --> 00:07:00,480
Understood.

116
00:07:04,240 --> 00:07:05,839
I understand, yes.

117
00:07:06,680 --> 00:07:08,160
See you next week then.

118
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:10,319
Right, will do.

119
00:07:10,519 --> 00:07:11,480
Goodbye. Goodbye.

120
00:07:50,959 --> 00:07:51,920
What brings you here?

121
00:07:52,800 --> 00:07:54,319
Something urgent has come up,

122
00:07:54,639 --> 00:07:55,680
and I need your help.

123
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:05,680
This inconspicuous little thing

124
00:08:05,720 --> 00:08:07,600
can pick up every word he says.

125
00:08:07,639 --> 00:08:09,800
We had one installed in his old office,

126
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:11,199
but he suddenly switched,

127
00:08:11,560 --> 00:08:13,000
saying the orientation wasn't right

128
00:08:13,079 --> 00:08:14,360
and wasn't as auspicious as the new one.

129
00:08:14,720 --> 00:08:15,439
In the next day or two,

130
00:08:15,480 --> 00:08:16,800
he has an important communication

131
00:08:16,959 --> 00:08:18,160
that must be monitored throughout.

132
00:08:18,519 --> 00:08:19,600
There's no time to send anyone else.

133
00:08:21,079 --> 00:08:21,879
You're the only one.

134
00:09:09,799 --> 00:09:10,720
Hello, President Lin.

135
00:09:12,240 --> 00:09:12,919
President Lin.

136
00:09:13,240 --> 00:09:13,919
President Lin.

137
00:09:24,919 --> 00:09:26,240
Before entering a room,

138
00:09:26,360 --> 00:09:28,320
you must have a mental map.

139
00:09:28,639 --> 00:09:30,360
The ideal spots for bugs

140
00:09:30,600 --> 00:09:31,960
share three things in common:

141
00:09:32,080 --> 00:09:32,799
Concealment,

142
00:09:33,120 --> 00:09:33,879
stability,

143
00:09:34,120 --> 00:09:35,039
and good acoustics.

144
00:09:36,919 --> 00:09:37,759
Hello, President Lin.

145
00:09:37,759 --> 00:09:38,840
President Lin. President Lin.

146
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:11,240
Hello, President Lin.

147
00:10:23,600 --> 00:10:24,080
Boss.

148
00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:25,600
I made you some tea.

149
00:10:26,519 --> 00:10:28,440
There's something I need to tell you.

150
00:10:29,120 --> 00:10:29,879
Hold on, hold on.

151
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:37,200
Who's this?

152
00:10:40,159 --> 00:10:41,200
The Red Cross.

153
00:10:45,639 --> 00:10:46,720
Who made the donation on my behalf?

154
00:10:49,559 --> 00:10:50,519
Mayor Xie.

155
00:10:55,360 --> 00:10:55,879
All right.

156
00:10:56,320 --> 00:10:56,919
Thank you.

157
00:11:08,279 --> 00:11:09,840
What were you going to tell me just now?

158
00:11:11,559 --> 00:11:14,240
A procurement worker came by earlier.

159
00:11:14,559 --> 00:11:17,080
He claimed he was framed.

160
00:11:17,960 --> 00:11:19,159
Someone accused him of taking kickbacks.

161
00:11:20,240 --> 00:11:21,240
Framed, my ass!

162
00:11:21,720 --> 00:11:23,799
If I can't spot fake corruption from real,

163
00:11:23,799 --> 00:11:24,679
I might as well quit.

164
00:11:26,879 --> 00:11:28,879
So should we fire him?

165
00:11:32,200 --> 00:11:33,679
Do you know Hai Rui from the Ming dynasty?

166
00:11:34,120 --> 00:11:34,840
Yes.

167
00:11:35,840 --> 00:11:36,679
What do you think of him?

168
00:11:37,799 --> 00:11:39,440
Upright and just.

169
00:11:40,519 --> 00:11:41,639
Just cared too much about his reputation.

170
00:11:42,519 --> 00:11:44,279
Caring about his reputation is a flaw.

171
00:11:44,720 --> 00:11:46,759
Being obsessed with praise from the people

172
00:11:47,320 --> 00:11:48,399
is a clear weakness.

173
00:11:48,720 --> 00:11:49,840
Treat the illness to save the patient.

174
00:11:50,320 --> 00:11:51,279
Why fire him?

175
00:11:52,639 --> 00:11:54,279
When I hire, I prefer people with flaws.

176
00:11:54,960 --> 00:11:56,159
I only worry when someone has none.

177
00:11:57,639 --> 00:12:00,639
Round up some workers tomorrow.

178
00:12:00,960 --> 00:12:01,840
Before 10:30,

179
00:12:01,840 --> 00:12:03,519
gather at the municipal government building.

180
00:12:04,519 --> 00:12:05,679
Mayor Xie is being transferred.

181
00:12:06,279 --> 00:12:08,039
Line up to give him a send-off.

182
00:12:08,519 --> 00:12:09,240
Remember,

183
00:12:09,279 --> 00:12:10,159
it must look spontaneous.

184
00:12:10,840 --> 00:12:12,279
If anyone can cry,

185
00:12:12,399 --> 00:12:13,720
shedding real tears would be best.

186
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:16,039
Also, bring plenty of local specialties.

187
00:12:16,200 --> 00:12:18,399
Stuff them into his car regardless.

188
00:12:18,399 --> 00:12:18,919
Okay.

189
00:12:26,200 --> 00:12:26,919
Understood?

190
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:27,639
Understood.

191
00:12:33,240 --> 00:12:35,679
Working hard also caters to his tastes.

192
00:12:49,919 --> 00:12:51,000
Hello, President Lin.

193
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:02,480
What's that loud noise?

194
00:13:05,799 --> 00:13:06,519
It's broken.

195
00:13:07,399 --> 00:13:08,679
Call someone to fix it right away.

196
00:13:09,039 --> 00:13:09,600
Okay.

197
00:13:10,879 --> 00:13:11,519
All right.

198
00:13:19,639 --> 00:13:20,759
Where were we?

199
00:13:21,279 --> 00:13:23,120
He says he's already divorced from us,

200
00:13:23,120 --> 00:13:25,159
and at most, we're just dating now.

201
00:13:25,240 --> 00:13:27,159
Discussion is fine, but don't give orders.

202
00:13:35,320 --> 00:13:36,840
At most, just be friends with him.

203
00:13:37,720 --> 00:13:39,320
He's made himself so complicated.

204
00:13:39,320 --> 00:13:40,720
Who would dare date him?

205
00:13:41,840 --> 00:13:43,200
Given his current status,

206
00:13:43,320 --> 00:13:44,519
are there any rules for using him?

207
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:46,559
After all, he used to be one of ours.

208
00:13:46,879 --> 00:13:48,679
"Serving our purpose" is the rule.

209
00:13:49,399 --> 00:13:50,960
Use him just like anyone else.

210
00:13:51,440 --> 00:13:52,320
Each takes what they need.

211
00:13:52,960 --> 00:13:53,960
Unless he...

212
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:55,519
commits treason.

213
00:14:38,639 --> 00:14:41,919
I'm retiring tomorrow.

214
00:14:42,639 --> 00:14:43,879
After midnight tonight,

215
00:14:44,159 --> 00:14:45,080
I'm unplugging my phone line.

216
00:14:45,519 --> 00:14:47,440
I'm catching up on decades of lost sleep.

217
00:14:47,960 --> 00:14:49,039
Don't any of you try to reach me.

218
00:14:49,399 --> 00:14:50,360
Don't disrupt my sleep.

219
00:14:51,360 --> 00:14:52,919
From the day I started working until now,

220
00:14:53,480 --> 00:14:55,200
I've followed many cases for decades.

221
00:14:55,840 --> 00:14:57,399
Some cases reached a full stop,

222
00:14:59,200 --> 00:15:01,080
but others are still just commas today.

223
00:15:02,080 --> 00:15:03,840
In some cases, the leads are still active.

224
00:15:04,399 --> 00:15:05,759
For others, the leads have gone cold.

225
00:15:06,519 --> 00:15:07,240
Especially

226
00:15:07,840 --> 00:15:08,720
from right after liberation—

227
00:15:08,720 --> 00:15:10,320
the spies in those old dossiers

228
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:12,000
might all be dead by now.

229
00:15:12,879 --> 00:15:13,440
Yet,

230
00:15:14,039 --> 00:15:16,039
new cases and new leads keep surfacing.

231
00:15:16,639 --> 00:15:18,480
That's the nature of intelligence work:

232
00:15:19,080 --> 00:15:19,759
drawn out,

233
00:15:20,240 --> 00:15:21,000
and tortuous.

234
00:15:23,039 --> 00:15:24,159
You're all young.

235
00:15:24,799 --> 00:15:25,799
You have to race against time

236
00:15:26,799 --> 00:15:27,519
and crack more cases.

237
00:15:31,559 --> 00:15:32,399
One last thing.

238
00:15:33,120 --> 00:15:34,159
Out of my pension,

239
00:15:34,159 --> 00:15:35,480
I'm putting up 15,000 yuan

240
00:15:35,720 --> 00:15:36,519
to leave with your division.

241
00:15:37,120 --> 00:15:39,320
Whoever sees the Lin Kanshan lead through,

242
00:15:39,919 --> 00:15:43,200
uncovers every single lead tied to him,

243
00:15:43,639 --> 00:15:44,320
every single person,

244
00:15:44,720 --> 00:15:45,600
busts them all in one fell swoop,

245
00:15:46,159 --> 00:15:48,639
and puts a perfect period on it—

246
00:15:49,399 --> 00:15:50,000
Old Wei,

247
00:15:50,759 --> 00:15:52,519
use this to buy them a large LCD color TV

248
00:15:52,799 --> 00:15:53,600
as a reward.

249
00:16:07,639 --> 00:16:08,440
Work hard.

250
00:16:55,679 --> 00:16:58,080
Sometimes your chosen spot is compromised.

251
00:16:58,399 --> 00:16:59,200
Don't panic.

252
00:16:59,200 --> 00:17:00,879
Fall back to your secondary location.

253
00:17:01,200 --> 00:17:02,440
For every operation,

254
00:17:02,440 --> 00:17:04,559
prepare at least three backup spots.

255
00:17:05,160 --> 00:17:06,440
Adjusting isn't failure.

256
00:17:07,160 --> 00:17:08,200
Rushing is.

257
00:17:13,279 --> 00:17:14,359
Hello, President Lin.

258
00:17:30,079 --> 00:17:30,920
You're back.

259
00:17:35,279 --> 00:17:36,200
Only apples?

260
00:17:37,680 --> 00:17:38,480
Where are the bananas?

261
00:17:38,519 --> 00:17:40,599
They're soft. Won't look good set out.

262
00:17:40,680 --> 00:17:42,279
Besides, this is no ordinary guest.

263
00:17:42,440 --> 00:17:43,440
What are you doing?

264
00:17:43,440 --> 00:17:44,200
Throwing it out.

265
00:17:44,240 --> 00:17:45,079
This one's rotten.

266
00:17:45,720 --> 00:17:47,079
It's fine.

267
00:17:47,079 --> 00:17:48,680
Wu Jinhe is hardly a stranger.

268
00:17:48,880 --> 00:17:49,599
Let me tell you,

269
00:17:49,599 --> 00:17:51,079
he won't even look at these,

270
00:17:51,119 --> 00:17:52,400
let alone eat them.

271
00:17:53,319 --> 00:17:54,480
This will do just fine.

272
00:17:56,119 --> 00:17:57,000
Hold on.

273
00:17:57,039 --> 00:17:58,799
Wait until the guest arrives to brew it.

274
00:17:58,799 --> 00:18:00,200
You don't even know if he likes it.

275
00:18:00,200 --> 00:18:01,720
Otherwise you'll have to brew it again.

276
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:06,240
Weren't there two open packets from before?

277
00:18:06,319 --> 00:18:06,920
Where are they?

278
00:18:06,960 --> 00:18:07,920
In the cabinet.

279
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:09,720
Just use the opened ones.

280
00:18:09,799 --> 00:18:11,319
Quick, swap them out.

281
00:18:20,079 --> 00:18:22,079
Hey brother, I've arrived.

282
00:18:22,160 --> 00:18:22,799
Alright, alright.

283
00:18:23,640 --> 00:18:25,079
I'll run right down.

284
00:18:42,160 --> 00:18:42,759
Hey, brother.

285
00:18:44,519 --> 00:18:45,279
Coming upstairs?

286
00:18:49,960 --> 00:18:51,400
Let's talk in the car. I have plans soon.

287
00:18:53,440 --> 00:18:55,960
Lin Zhaodi. "Zhao" as in bringing wealth,

288
00:18:55,960 --> 00:18:56,960
and "di" with the female radical.

289
00:18:57,119 --> 00:18:58,480
It was originally those two characters.

290
00:18:58,880 --> 00:18:59,440
I don't know if

291
00:18:59,440 --> 00:19:01,240
the registry clerk made a typo,

292
00:19:01,240 --> 00:19:02,400
or what went wrong,

293
00:19:02,799 --> 00:19:05,200
but on her ID, "di" became "brother".

294
00:19:05,279 --> 00:19:06,839
That made her impossible to track down.

295
00:19:08,160 --> 00:19:09,319
Now there's a lead.

296
00:19:09,319 --> 00:19:10,680
Just like you said,

297
00:19:10,680 --> 00:19:12,359
a town in Yongtai.

298
00:19:12,519 --> 00:19:16,319
Rumor is she moved again after liberation.

299
00:19:16,359 --> 00:19:18,160
Some say she went back to her old home,

300
00:19:18,160 --> 00:19:20,200
while others said she went to Jiangxi.

301
00:19:20,240 --> 00:19:21,799
Either way, with her old fellow villagers,

302
00:19:21,799 --> 00:19:22,839
she lost all contact.

303
00:19:22,839 --> 00:19:23,680
I'll keep looking.

304
00:19:23,680 --> 00:19:25,680
There are things I don't dare tell my dad.

305
00:19:25,880 --> 00:19:27,960
We don't even know if she's still alive.

306
00:19:28,039 --> 00:19:30,240
She's so old, but we have to keep looking.

307
00:19:30,240 --> 00:19:31,599
Otherwise, I can't answer to him.

308
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:33,759
In just a few decades,

309
00:19:34,359 --> 00:19:35,440
there's been so much turmoil and moving.

310
00:19:36,119 --> 00:19:37,279
A lot of people from the older generation,

311
00:19:37,279 --> 00:19:39,240
weren't they all drifting around like that?

312
00:19:39,240 --> 00:19:41,160
Wasn't Mayor Xie's mother-in-law the same?

313
00:19:41,240 --> 00:19:43,279
She spent years searching for her roots.

314
00:19:44,599 --> 00:19:46,160
He should be called Chairman Xie now.

315
00:19:46,400 --> 00:19:48,480
His style is totally different these days.

316
00:19:48,680 --> 00:19:50,559
Before, no minor issue waited overnight.

317
00:19:50,920 --> 00:19:54,160
Now fixing a toilet needs a Party meeting.

318
00:19:54,279 --> 00:19:55,880
Playing it safe has its perks.

319
00:19:56,200 --> 00:19:58,759
It's secure. Isn't that what life's about?

320
00:19:58,759 --> 00:20:00,839
When it's time to charge, you charge ahead.

321
00:20:01,359 --> 00:20:02,880
But you can't keep charging all the time.

322
00:20:03,640 --> 00:20:04,880
Pace yourself.

323
00:20:05,119 --> 00:20:06,359
What if you take a bad fall?

324
00:20:08,559 --> 00:20:10,359
Keep your eyes wide open, brother.

325
00:20:27,400 --> 00:20:28,279
In news from our station:

326
00:20:28,640 --> 00:20:29,440
On the morning of the sixth,

327
00:20:29,440 --> 00:20:31,839
Ronghai Aerospace Technology Co., Ltd.'s

328
00:20:31,839 --> 00:20:33,680
new chairman, Xie Fengshi,

329
00:20:34,039 --> 00:20:36,599
at the Provincial High-Tech Industry Conference,

330
00:20:36,680 --> 00:20:37,720
delivered an address,

331
00:20:37,720 --> 00:20:40,480
stating that in the second half, the company will focus

332
00:20:40,480 --> 00:20:41,599
on its core mission and primary business,

333
00:20:41,880 --> 00:20:44,599
speed up commercializing aerospace results,

334
00:20:44,920 --> 00:20:48,119
and strive for breakthroughs in commercial aerospace.

335
00:20:48,720 --> 00:20:51,160
Ronghai Aerospace Technology Co., Ltd.

336
00:20:51,160 --> 00:20:52,960
was founded in 1986,

337
00:20:53,440 --> 00:20:55,880
and was among the first market entities

338
00:20:55,880 --> 00:20:58,359
to industrialize aerospace technology.

339
00:21:30,960 --> 00:21:33,240
Secretary Jin, we're done for the day.

340
00:22:51,319 --> 00:22:52,160
What's wrong with the curtains?

341
00:22:53,400 --> 00:22:54,440
Aren't you off work?

342
00:22:54,680 --> 00:22:55,920
Why did you come back?

343
00:22:56,200 --> 00:22:57,720
This bracket isn't sturdy.

344
00:22:58,119 --> 00:23:00,599
The curtains are too heavy. It can't hold.

345
00:23:01,440 --> 00:23:03,240
It got pulled right out of the wall.

346
00:23:07,319 --> 00:23:09,039
Can you screw it back in?

347
00:23:09,319 --> 00:23:10,079
I can.

348
00:23:16,839 --> 00:23:18,440
You can't handle this job.

349
00:23:18,440 --> 00:23:19,240
Let me try.

350
00:23:19,720 --> 00:23:21,240
If I let go, it'll fall.

351
00:23:21,240 --> 00:23:23,079
Just get down when I tell you.

352
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:25,519
Without screws, it'll fall anyway.

353
00:23:49,119 --> 00:23:50,240
Weren't you ignoring me?

354
00:23:51,319 --> 00:23:52,440
Weren't you mad at me?

355
00:23:54,079 --> 00:23:55,319
Not giving me a hard time today?

356
00:23:58,960 --> 00:24:00,200
Couldn't help yourself?

357
00:24:16,759 --> 00:24:19,319
This is the Xiamen head of the California

358
00:24:19,319 --> 00:24:21,440
Aerospace 2019 Project, Mr. Ginsberg.

359
00:24:22,240 --> 00:24:23,279
Looking forward to working with you.

360
00:24:23,519 --> 00:24:24,519
And these two are...

361
00:24:24,519 --> 00:24:27,319
renowned aerospace propulsion expert Elena,

362
00:24:27,519 --> 00:24:30,119
and aviation materials expert Ms. Connie.

363
00:24:30,640 --> 00:24:31,160
Hello.

364
00:24:31,720 --> 00:24:32,599
Pleasure to meet you.

365
00:24:33,319 --> 00:24:34,640
Oh right, almost forgot the last one.

366
00:24:34,640 --> 00:24:35,759
Our last guest is...

367
00:24:35,799 --> 00:24:37,920
Outai International Group's special rep,

368
00:24:38,079 --> 00:24:38,880
Mr. George.

369
00:24:38,880 --> 00:24:40,880
He also has a Chinese name, Qiao Liang.

370
00:24:42,400 --> 00:24:45,160
In China, a bridge is a bond

371
00:24:45,160 --> 00:24:46,480
that fosters friendship.

372
00:24:46,920 --> 00:24:48,359
Who gave you that Chinese name?

373
00:24:48,359 --> 00:24:50,960
I lived in Beijing for many years.

374
00:24:50,960 --> 00:24:53,400
An old man in a hutong gave it to me.

375
00:24:54,880 --> 00:24:56,799
He said, "Never mind all that.

376
00:24:56,799 --> 00:24:58,599
The key is that it's easy to remember."

377
00:25:00,200 --> 00:25:01,200
Great, welcome, everyone.

378
00:25:01,319 --> 00:25:03,039
Come, please sit down. Have a seat.

379
00:25:04,039 --> 00:25:04,920
Mr. Xie.

380
00:25:05,279 --> 00:25:07,319
When you studied in the US,

381
00:25:07,359 --> 00:25:09,079
you had a classmate,

382
00:25:09,440 --> 00:25:10,640
Ning Li from California.

383
00:25:10,759 --> 00:25:13,440
He said you once gave him...

384
00:25:13,519 --> 00:25:15,640
a Chinese nickname: "Shorty."

385
00:25:16,920 --> 00:25:17,880
Do you remember?

386
00:25:17,880 --> 00:25:19,160
He happens to be my uncle.

387
00:25:19,319 --> 00:25:20,319
What a coincidence!

388
00:25:20,319 --> 00:25:21,799
Haven't seen him in so many years.

389
00:25:21,880 --> 00:25:22,640
How has he been?

390
00:25:22,720 --> 00:25:26,480
He asked me to tell you he misses you dearly.

391
00:25:27,799 --> 00:25:28,319
Good, that's wonderful.

392
00:25:28,359 --> 00:25:29,440
Come, please take a seat.

393
00:25:33,119 --> 00:25:33,759
Chairman.

394
00:25:34,680 --> 00:25:36,480
Mr. Qiao Liang asked to see you privately.

395
00:25:36,640 --> 00:25:38,359
Would you like me to arrange that?

396
00:25:38,599 --> 00:25:40,319
Just say I'm at a provincial Party meeting.

397
00:25:40,319 --> 00:25:41,440
See them off for me later.

398
00:25:42,079 --> 00:25:43,480
He asked me to hand you a letter.

399
00:25:43,759 --> 00:25:44,759
He said his uncle wrote it.

400
00:25:45,160 --> 00:25:45,640
All right.

401
00:25:46,240 --> 00:25:46,960
Make sure to entertain them well.

402
00:25:46,960 --> 00:25:47,359
Will do.

403
00:26:06,400 --> 00:26:09,640
My uncle said once you read that letter,

404
00:26:09,839 --> 00:26:11,359
you'd likely meet with me.

405
00:26:11,519 --> 00:26:12,640
"But you must wait

406
00:26:12,680 --> 00:26:15,440
until you have a private meeting like this

407
00:26:15,440 --> 00:26:18,400
before I hand over the second letter."

408
00:26:18,400 --> 00:26:20,599
If it suits you,

409
00:26:20,880 --> 00:26:22,160
within half a month,

410
00:26:22,279 --> 00:26:25,039
your whole family can receive green cards.

411
00:26:25,519 --> 00:26:29,440
If you dislike the terms in the letter,

412
00:26:29,640 --> 00:26:30,759
bring them up now,

413
00:26:30,759 --> 00:26:32,720
and I can deliver them right now.

414
00:26:36,279 --> 00:26:38,839
Shorty has quite a gift for languages,

415
00:26:40,880 --> 00:26:42,480
but there is one word

416
00:26:42,680 --> 00:26:43,960
he might not understand well:

417
00:26:44,119 --> 00:26:45,039
"traitor."

418
00:26:47,720 --> 00:26:48,799
This isn't helping me.

419
00:26:49,759 --> 00:26:52,240
He wants to put his old classmate in jail.

420
00:26:52,319 --> 00:26:54,559
Just as a consultant.

421
00:26:54,720 --> 00:26:57,799
A consultant who only answers yes or no.

422
00:26:58,519 --> 00:27:01,759
The shady, underhanded work...

423
00:27:01,759 --> 00:27:04,599
We'd never expect you to do that yourself.

424
00:27:04,599 --> 00:27:05,160
If...

425
00:27:05,160 --> 00:27:05,960
Xiao Lyu.

426
00:27:07,200 --> 00:27:07,920
Xiao Lyu!

427
00:27:12,720 --> 00:27:13,799
I'm not afraid

428
00:27:13,799 --> 00:27:16,359
of others discovering my identity.

429
00:27:16,839 --> 00:27:19,680
But if the provincial committee learns

430
00:27:19,680 --> 00:27:22,000
that you're meeting with someone like me,

431
00:27:24,440 --> 00:27:26,720
it might be hard to explain.

432
00:27:34,160 --> 00:27:35,799
Chairman, did you call for me?

433
00:27:37,720 --> 00:27:39,319
Call the provincial Party committee duty office.

434
00:27:39,319 --> 00:27:40,559
Tell them that right now,

435
00:27:40,559 --> 00:27:42,559
I'm meeting a very important foreign guest,

436
00:27:43,559 --> 00:27:46,559
and have Discipline and Inspection Committee comrades attend.

437
00:28:25,880 --> 00:28:26,880
Weren't you ignoring me?

438
00:28:27,519 --> 00:28:28,720
Weren't you mad at me?

439
00:28:29,359 --> 00:28:30,799
Not picking a fight with me today?

440
00:28:55,279 --> 00:28:56,000
Come in.

441
00:28:56,240 --> 00:28:57,039
Boss.

442
00:29:08,680 --> 00:29:09,319
Boss,

443
00:29:13,680 --> 00:29:14,799
There's a document

444
00:29:14,799 --> 00:29:16,079
that needs your signature.

445
00:29:20,880 --> 00:29:21,480
What's wrong?

446
00:29:22,559 --> 00:29:24,599
Why is there a screw missing?

447
00:29:25,880 --> 00:29:27,720
I asked the handyman this morning.

448
00:29:27,720 --> 00:29:30,200
He said it needs an expansion bolt.

449
00:29:30,200 --> 00:29:31,519
He looked everywhere but couldn't find one,

450
00:29:31,559 --> 00:29:32,880
spent ages and still couldn't fix it,

451
00:29:32,880 --> 00:29:33,960
and said he'd come back tonight.

452
00:29:36,839 --> 00:29:38,319
Look at how these people work,

453
00:29:38,680 --> 00:29:39,799
just dragging their feet.

454
00:29:40,720 --> 00:29:41,960
Employing all these people,

455
00:29:41,960 --> 00:29:43,400
they're all good for nothing.

456
00:29:49,400 --> 00:29:50,240
Go get back to work.

457
00:29:51,400 --> 00:29:52,000
Alright.

458
00:29:58,599 --> 00:30:00,599
Don't touch the curtain box spot.

459
00:30:00,920 --> 00:30:03,839
A cleaner will come in later to handle it.

460
00:30:04,039 --> 00:30:06,240
Your mission is perimeter support.

461
00:30:07,000 --> 00:30:08,759
Make sure during that time window,

462
00:30:09,119 --> 00:30:11,079
keep unauthorized people out of the hall.

463
00:30:12,319 --> 00:30:13,079
Remember,

464
00:30:13,480 --> 00:30:14,880
cover isn't a performance.

465
00:30:15,599 --> 00:30:17,119
It's about controlling variables.

466
00:31:39,640 --> 00:31:41,200
I've gathered all the study materials for you.

467
00:31:41,279 --> 00:31:42,319
As long as you pass the written exam,

468
00:31:42,319 --> 00:31:44,160
you'll pretty much be set for the interview.

469
00:31:44,160 --> 00:31:45,440
It's just the civil service exam, after all.

470
00:31:45,440 --> 00:31:47,640
It all comes down to these materials.

471
00:31:47,680 --> 00:31:48,720
It's not complicated.

472
00:31:49,000 --> 00:31:50,200
Just dive in,

473
00:31:50,440 --> 00:31:52,640
study for a few months, and that'll be enough.

474
00:31:53,559 --> 00:31:55,960
Have you decided which agency to apply for?

475
00:32:06,200 --> 00:32:08,480
You could consider the Municipal State Security Bureau.

476
00:32:08,480 --> 00:32:09,400
The Provincial Department is also good.

477
00:32:09,400 --> 00:32:10,480
Agencies like these

478
00:32:10,480 --> 00:32:11,960
just keep a lower profile.

479
00:32:11,960 --> 00:32:13,599
An iron rice bowl—stable,

480
00:32:13,599 --> 00:32:15,079
and it meets your family's expectations.

481
00:32:15,079 --> 00:32:16,359
Allowances for business trips

482
00:32:16,359 --> 00:32:18,319
or regular overtime

483
00:32:18,319 --> 00:32:19,880
are higher than at other agencies.

484
00:32:19,880 --> 00:32:20,920
What do you think?

485
00:32:32,279 --> 00:32:33,440
I didn't hear it earlier.

486
00:32:33,440 --> 00:32:34,559
I was on the road.

487
00:32:34,599 --> 00:32:35,240
What's up?

488
00:32:35,240 --> 00:32:37,440
Your uncle's classmate was right next to me.

489
00:32:37,440 --> 00:32:39,039
He's the head of a major enterprise.

490
00:32:39,079 --> 00:32:40,559
I told you last time,

491
00:32:40,599 --> 00:32:42,200
you can go work for him in the future.

492
00:32:42,200 --> 00:32:44,240
I called so you could say a few words,

493
00:32:44,240 --> 00:32:45,720
called repeatedly, but you didn't answer.

494
00:32:45,720 --> 00:32:47,000
As for that girlfriend of yours,

495
00:32:47,000 --> 00:32:48,279
don't bring her up anymore.

496
00:32:48,279 --> 00:32:49,440
Neither your father nor I approve.

497
00:32:49,759 --> 00:32:51,039
You just got home today.

498
00:32:51,240 --> 00:32:53,319
I don't want this to cause any friction.

499
00:32:53,480 --> 00:32:54,400
See you in a bit.

500
00:33:01,400 --> 00:33:02,359
Actually,

501
00:33:03,160 --> 00:33:04,559
I'm not as important as you think.

502
00:33:07,920 --> 00:33:10,039
Young people have a limitless future.

503
00:33:10,039 --> 00:33:11,599
This is just the beginning.

504
00:33:12,000 --> 00:33:13,599
You'll surely rise through the ranks.

505
00:33:16,200 --> 00:33:17,799
Have some confidence.

506
00:33:24,400 --> 00:33:25,400
Just make do with this.

507
00:33:25,440 --> 00:33:26,680
Did you add the seasoning packet?

508
00:33:26,680 --> 00:33:27,680
Just one packet.

509
00:33:27,680 --> 00:33:29,680
Didn't the doctor tell you to cut back on salt?

510
00:33:30,319 --> 00:33:31,319
All right.

511
00:33:31,319 --> 00:33:32,480
For my health.

512
00:33:35,799 --> 00:33:37,920
Read this afternoon's provincial briefing?

513
00:33:38,200 --> 00:33:39,359
Regarding Xie Fengshi?

514
00:33:39,960 --> 00:33:42,240
The Americans made a recruitment approach,

515
00:33:42,240 --> 00:33:43,200
offering him a green card.

516
00:33:44,279 --> 00:33:45,000
What do you think?

517
00:33:45,759 --> 00:33:47,680
My brother-in-law, Wu Jinhe,

518
00:33:47,880 --> 00:33:48,759
you've met him before.

519
00:33:48,759 --> 00:33:50,119
He and Qian Xinfu,

520
00:33:50,119 --> 00:33:52,720
never liked each other at work to begin with.

521
00:33:53,039 --> 00:33:55,279
This time, competing for the same position,

522
00:33:55,279 --> 00:33:57,079
their relationship became toxic.

523
00:33:57,160 --> 00:33:58,160
They reported each other.

524
00:33:58,440 --> 00:33:59,160
Thanks.

525
00:33:59,160 --> 00:34:00,480
They almost came to blows.

526
00:34:00,480 --> 00:34:01,400
Last week,

527
00:34:01,400 --> 00:34:03,119
Qian Xinfu reported my brother-in-law,

528
00:34:03,119 --> 00:34:04,720
claiming he had a child out of wedlock.

529
00:34:05,319 --> 00:34:07,200
Which was completely impossible, of course.

530
00:34:07,559 --> 00:34:08,280
Yet,

531
00:34:08,280 --> 00:34:10,480
the organization has reservations about

532
00:34:10,559 --> 00:34:11,440
the promotion of compromised officials.

533
00:34:12,239 --> 00:34:14,280
It's actually the same for Xie Fengshi.

534
00:34:14,320 --> 00:34:15,119
Logically speaking,

535
00:34:15,119 --> 00:34:16,559
he rejected the US attempt to turn him.

536
00:34:16,559 --> 00:34:18,119
That should be a good thing.

537
00:34:18,119 --> 00:34:19,199
But if the provincial authorities learn

538
00:34:19,199 --> 00:34:20,519
he had contact with spies,

539
00:34:20,519 --> 00:34:22,360
it will definitely hurt his promotion.

540
00:34:22,679 --> 00:34:24,519
Fortunately, he reported it in time.

541
00:34:28,719 --> 00:34:29,440
Go on.

542
00:34:33,000 --> 00:34:34,760
Cadres approached by spies

543
00:34:35,000 --> 00:34:36,760
shouldn't be marginalized by their units,

544
00:34:36,760 --> 00:34:38,159
nor should they face a blanket policy.

545
00:34:38,239 --> 00:34:41,360
Otherwise we fail to save one of our own.

546
00:34:42,239 --> 00:34:43,079
Besides,

547
00:34:43,079 --> 00:34:45,519
I think those cultivated by spies,

548
00:34:46,079 --> 00:34:47,760
or who are already turned,

549
00:34:47,920 --> 00:34:49,480
if there's no real need to wait,

550
00:34:49,480 --> 00:34:50,760
we should stop them promptly.

551
00:34:50,800 --> 00:34:52,880
We don't have to wait until making an arrest.

552
00:34:52,880 --> 00:34:54,159
Because the longer it drags on,

553
00:34:54,159 --> 00:34:55,800
the greater our losses will be.

554
00:34:59,400 --> 00:35:00,599
Based on these two points,

555
00:35:00,599 --> 00:35:01,760
draft a report.

556
00:35:01,960 --> 00:35:03,320
I'll submit it to the provincial department right away.

557
00:35:03,800 --> 00:35:04,519
One more thing.

558
00:35:04,639 --> 00:35:07,239
Chen Shui-bian has been teetering lately.

559
00:35:07,239 --> 00:35:08,719
We must prevent Taiwan, China

560
00:35:08,719 --> 00:35:11,239
from infiltrating these key secure units.

561
00:35:11,239 --> 00:35:14,480
Organize security training in staggered batches.

562
00:35:14,760 --> 00:35:15,559
Understood.

563
00:35:15,559 --> 00:35:16,840
Strike the right balance.

564
00:35:17,039 --> 00:35:18,800
Don't let a warning turn into a tip-off.

565
00:35:27,199 --> 00:35:28,159
In our country,

566
00:35:28,159 --> 00:35:29,800
it refers to the People's Bank of China

567
00:35:30,039 --> 00:35:32,280
aiming to achieve specific economic goals

568
00:35:32,280 --> 00:35:33,760
by using various tools

569
00:35:33,760 --> 00:35:36,559
to adjust money supply and interest rates,

570
00:35:36,559 --> 00:35:39,639
influencing macroeconomic operations

571
00:35:39,639 --> 00:35:41,960
through overall policies and measures.

572
00:35:41,960 --> 00:35:43,039
To use an analogy,

573
00:35:43,480 --> 00:35:46,280
if capital and money are water,

574
00:35:46,320 --> 00:35:49,119
then monetary policy is the reservoir's floodgate.

575
00:35:49,599 --> 00:35:52,280
Monetary easing means opening the gate

576
00:35:52,320 --> 00:35:53,440
to let the water flow out.

577
00:35:53,519 --> 00:35:56,400
Monetary tightening means shutting the gate tight,

578
00:35:56,519 --> 00:35:58,440
keeping the water where it is.

579
00:35:58,440 --> 00:36:00,280
Specifically at the government level,

580
00:36:00,280 --> 00:36:02,280
if monetary policy is well-crafted,

581
00:36:02,360 --> 00:36:03,639
it stimulates consumption,

582
00:36:03,639 --> 00:36:05,199
boosts economic growth,

583
00:36:05,199 --> 00:36:07,559
and addresses rising unemployment.

584
00:36:07,599 --> 00:36:09,079
If it's poorly formulated,

585
00:36:09,119 --> 00:36:10,599
minor troubles aside,

586
00:36:10,599 --> 00:36:14,159
at worst, it impacts the national economy.

587
00:36:14,159 --> 00:36:15,039
Wait a moment.

588
00:36:15,440 --> 00:36:16,480
Do you have a question?

589
00:36:16,880 --> 00:36:19,480
Let's close that window a bit first.

590
00:36:19,760 --> 00:36:20,840
It's too windy.

591
00:36:20,840 --> 00:36:23,000
We wouldn't want such insights blown away,

592
00:36:23,000 --> 00:36:24,440
going in through one ear

593
00:36:24,440 --> 00:36:25,840
and right out the other.

594
00:36:29,119 --> 00:36:30,440
You explained that so well!

595
00:36:30,960 --> 00:36:32,480
We really have a lot to learn from you.

596
00:36:33,079 --> 00:36:33,719
You flatter me.

597
00:36:33,719 --> 00:36:34,639
Vice Governor Wu.

598
00:36:34,920 --> 00:36:36,880
Well, Professor Pan, you're always welcome

599
00:36:36,880 --> 00:36:38,079
to come by often and share your insights.

600
00:36:38,079 --> 00:36:39,760
All right, thank you, Vice Governor Wu.

601
00:36:49,000 --> 00:36:49,800
Thank you, Professor Pan.

602
00:36:49,800 --> 00:36:50,800
It was my pleasure.

603
00:36:51,039 --> 00:36:51,480
See you next time.

604
00:36:51,480 --> 00:36:51,960
Okay, thank you.

605
00:36:51,960 --> 00:36:52,559
Take care.

606
00:36:53,079 --> 00:36:53,440
Okay.

607
00:36:58,119 --> 00:36:59,079
It seems Vice Governor Wu

608
00:36:59,079 --> 00:37:00,519
hasn't had enough of your lectures.

609
00:37:00,519 --> 00:37:02,239
When is he planning to invite you back?

610
00:37:02,239 --> 00:37:03,480
He didn't give me a date.

611
00:37:03,480 --> 00:37:05,000
Though I'm fully booked this week.

612
00:37:05,000 --> 00:37:05,639
When the leadership pays attention,

613
00:37:05,639 --> 00:37:06,679
the subordinates have to follow suit.

614
00:37:06,679 --> 00:37:07,880
When will you give a lecture at my place?

615
00:37:07,920 --> 00:37:09,480
Definitely not this month.

616
00:37:09,719 --> 00:37:11,800
Have your secretary call my student at the end of the month.

617
00:37:11,800 --> 00:37:12,320
Sounds good.

618
00:37:12,320 --> 00:37:12,760
Okay.

619
00:37:24,159 --> 00:37:26,159
Your home, your office,

620
00:37:26,239 --> 00:37:27,840
and your house back in your hometown—we searched them all.

621
00:37:28,039 --> 00:37:29,639
Add up the money in your bank accounts,

622
00:37:30,079 --> 00:37:31,920
and it doesn't match Taiwan, China's payout.

623
00:37:32,599 --> 00:37:33,960
They only met you three times in total.

624
00:37:33,960 --> 00:37:35,159
There's no way they gave you that much money.

625
00:37:35,880 --> 00:37:37,840
So you have another channel for selling intelligence.

626
00:37:38,320 --> 00:37:39,360
We need to know his

627
00:37:39,360 --> 00:37:41,159
identity, background, and name.

628
00:37:41,639 --> 00:37:42,320
Don't hold anything back.

629
00:37:42,719 --> 00:37:44,480
This is your only chance at redemption.

630
00:37:44,800 --> 00:37:46,039
If you lie now,

631
00:37:46,480 --> 00:37:47,800
you suffered these six days for nothing.

632
00:37:47,800 --> 00:37:50,239
I stayed quiet, fearing a worse sentence.

633
00:37:50,360 --> 00:37:51,559
But as for what this person looks like,

634
00:37:51,559 --> 00:37:52,800
I really have no idea.

635
00:37:52,880 --> 00:37:54,440
If you didn't meet, how did you make the handoffs?

636
00:37:54,760 --> 00:37:55,599
A mailbox.

637
00:37:56,079 --> 00:37:57,440
Not an email inbox.

638
00:37:57,519 --> 00:37:59,880
A discarded post office mailbox.

639
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:02,280
There's one in front of the defunct towel factory.

640
00:38:02,679 --> 00:38:04,400
He told me to put the documents inside,

641
00:38:04,440 --> 00:38:05,559
and he'd pick them up the next day.

642
00:38:06,760 --> 00:38:08,159
You've written novels online,

643
00:38:08,159 --> 00:38:08,960
written blogs,

644
00:38:09,039 --> 00:38:10,159
and hacked other people's hard drives.

645
00:38:10,400 --> 00:38:12,400
That proves you're a highly curious person.

646
00:38:12,559 --> 00:38:14,119
So you definitely hid nearby

647
00:38:14,320 --> 00:38:15,079
and spied on him.

648
00:38:15,159 --> 00:38:17,840
Every time, he carried an umbrella and wore a hat.

649
00:38:17,960 --> 00:38:19,400
I couldn't see his face at all.

650
00:38:19,960 --> 00:38:21,559
The day after you dropped off the intel,

651
00:38:21,559 --> 00:38:22,639
did it always rain?

652
00:38:24,079 --> 00:38:24,480
Yes.

653
00:38:30,320 --> 00:38:31,159
"Where have you been,

654
00:38:31,159 --> 00:38:32,159
looking so disheveled?"

655
00:38:33,360 --> 00:38:34,559
"I went to tail someone."

656
00:38:35,679 --> 00:38:36,599
"Did it have to be today?"

657
00:38:37,760 --> 00:38:39,960
"No choice. He chose today."

658
00:38:40,480 --> 00:38:42,719
"Meeting in the rain leaves no trace."

659
00:38:45,400 --> 00:38:46,800
You even followed him.

660
00:38:47,079 --> 00:38:48,719
Wanted to see what car he took, where he went,

661
00:38:48,719 --> 00:38:50,159
and what he did, right?

662
00:38:50,159 --> 00:38:51,599
I couldn't keep up with him at all.

663
00:38:51,800 --> 00:38:54,000
After just a few alleys, he shook me off.

664
00:38:54,079 --> 00:38:55,920
Did he smell of disinfectant?

665
00:38:56,039 --> 00:38:58,239
Always beat the yellow light at crossings?

666
00:38:58,239 --> 00:38:59,559
Never looked back while walking?

667
00:39:00,360 --> 00:39:01,599
How did you know?

668
00:39:02,079 --> 00:39:03,519
Because he knew you were tailing him.

669
00:39:03,519 --> 00:39:04,159
But he didn't care,

670
00:39:04,159 --> 00:39:05,360
because he knew you couldn't keep up.

671
00:39:06,079 --> 00:39:07,599
He gave you so much money,

672
00:39:07,840 --> 00:39:10,039
proving you made multiple deals.

673
00:39:10,639 --> 00:39:12,400
A year of deals without showing his face

674
00:39:12,800 --> 00:39:14,639
means he never considered you a friend,

675
00:39:14,800 --> 00:39:16,119
and thought you held no real value.

676
00:39:16,760 --> 00:39:18,039
Someone that calculating...

677
00:39:20,519 --> 00:39:21,239
There's only one.

678
00:40:27,920 --> 00:40:29,239
There's a memory card inside.

679
00:40:29,800 --> 00:40:31,840
The password is the date we first met.

680
00:40:32,159 --> 00:40:33,639
Year, month, day.

681
00:40:33,920 --> 00:40:35,079
Don't do it the American way.

682
00:40:35,079 --> 00:40:36,400
Follow Chinese customs.

683
00:40:38,000 --> 00:40:40,239
I thought you wouldn't come out to meet me.

684
00:40:40,719 --> 00:40:44,840
Here's the password for your new US account.

685
00:40:48,119 --> 00:40:49,800
All your money is in there.

686
00:40:53,400 --> 00:40:54,440
You know, brother,

687
00:40:54,920 --> 00:40:57,400
just fill out a form,

688
00:40:57,800 --> 00:40:58,719
take an oath,

689
00:40:59,079 --> 00:41:00,559
and join us.

690
00:41:01,000 --> 00:41:04,599
Isn't this the best time to invite you?

691
00:41:05,199 --> 00:41:07,320
Why do you bother with these formalities?

692
00:41:07,360 --> 00:41:09,000
This formality...

693
00:41:09,079 --> 00:41:11,559
helps me know who's truly on my side.

694
00:41:11,639 --> 00:41:12,719
If I wanted to,

695
00:41:12,719 --> 00:41:15,159
I'd have filled out forms for a dozen agencies already.

696
00:41:15,440 --> 00:41:16,440
To be blunt,

697
00:41:17,960 --> 00:41:19,440
none of them are worth my time.

698
00:41:20,880 --> 00:41:21,719
Fair enough.

699
00:41:21,880 --> 00:41:22,639
I get it.

700
00:41:22,719 --> 00:41:24,719
Forget the form, then.

701
00:41:25,280 --> 00:41:29,199
Ronghai has an economist, Pan Xiaoying.

702
00:41:29,360 --> 00:41:30,760
You must know her, right?

703
00:41:31,400 --> 00:41:32,760
Help me turn her.

704
00:41:33,440 --> 00:41:35,320
I won't haggle with you on the price.

705
00:41:39,039 --> 00:41:40,719
Coming to me to buy intel is fine.

706
00:41:40,880 --> 00:41:42,599
As for turning people, forget it.

707
00:41:42,840 --> 00:41:43,719
Come on, brother.

708
00:41:43,719 --> 00:41:45,880
Your intel is so expensive.

709
00:41:46,239 --> 00:41:47,920
C-Cut me a deal.

710
00:41:47,920 --> 00:41:49,920
So I have something to show my bosses.

711
00:41:50,159 --> 00:41:52,199
Think it's too pricey? Trade intel for it, then.

712
00:41:53,239 --> 00:41:54,639
Chen Shui-bian is shooting his mouth off.

713
00:41:54,639 --> 00:41:56,400
Where do you Americans stand on this next?

714
00:41:56,639 --> 00:41:57,519
Once you have something,

715
00:41:57,519 --> 00:41:58,599
just email me.

716
00:41:59,079 --> 00:41:59,840
All right.

717
00:42:01,199 --> 00:42:02,440
Coffee's on you today.

718
00:42:02,800 --> 00:42:03,400
I'm off.

719
00:42:15,119 --> 00:42:16,159
May peace be upon you.

720
00:42:17,159 --> 00:42:18,159
Take a look.

721
00:42:31,239 --> 00:42:32,920
Here's what you deposited.

722
00:42:35,840 --> 00:42:36,639
Thank you.

723
00:42:36,639 --> 00:42:37,440
Goodbye.

724
00:42:55,280 --> 00:42:56,360
Still on a business trip, huh?

725
00:42:56,920 --> 00:42:57,960
Distance doesn't matter.

726
00:42:58,440 --> 00:42:59,199
If we need to meet,

727
00:42:59,199 --> 00:43:00,840
I can be right there tomorrow.

728
00:43:01,039 --> 00:43:03,000
So, did you get what I wanted?

729
00:43:08,400 --> 00:43:09,480
I'm Wang Kai,

730
00:43:09,480 --> 00:43:11,199
inviting you to watch the drama series

731
00:43:11,199 --> 00:43:12,119
*Confrontation*.

732
00:43:12,119 --> 00:43:12,880
Top-secret data.

733
00:43:12,880 --> 00:43:14,440
That's an engineer's lifeblood.

734
00:43:14,559 --> 00:43:16,360
To make them gouge out their lifeblood—

735
00:43:16,360 --> 00:43:17,800
of course it's going to be hard.

736
00:43:17,800 --> 00:43:20,000
If a wiretap might be compromised,

737
00:43:20,000 --> 00:43:21,400
assume it already is.

738
00:43:21,400 --> 00:43:22,639
Don't ever touch it again.

739
00:43:22,639 --> 00:43:24,239
Just pretend you know nothing at all.

740
00:43:24,239 --> 00:43:26,519
If He Chunxiao shows up here,

741
00:43:26,519 --> 00:43:27,960
it proves that he, Qiu Tian,

742
00:43:27,960 --> 00:43:28,559
and Jinlan

743
00:43:28,559 --> 00:43:30,079
are in cahoots.

744
00:43:30,079 --> 00:43:31,400
You deliberately had me cross the courtyard

745
00:43:31,400 --> 00:43:32,559
to play along in your little show.

746
00:43:32,559 --> 00:43:33,559
Who was that for?

747
00:43:33,559 --> 00:43:35,280
I might not know what your plan is,

748
00:43:35,280 --> 00:43:36,440
but

749
00:43:36,440 --> 00:43:38,000
I don't mind letting you owe me a favor.
